{"chunk_id":"R1-2210919-001","collection":"ran1_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["HiSilicon","Nokia","Huawei"],"tdocNumber":"R1-2210919","title":"Discussion on cases for prioritization related to PUSCH in TS 38.213 and TS 38.214"},"point_id":"15692021165134400078"}
In this paper we are discussing the specification for intra-UE prioritization related to SP-CSI. According to companies’ views given in last meeting [1], it was generally found that the current specification describes this operation in a far too complicated manner, since it requires parallel reading of TS 38.213 and TS 38.214 and also relies on conclusions for some cases, whereas the handling of other cases can be obtained either from 38.213 (section 9) or from TS 38.214 (Section 5.2.5). To overcome this problem, two TPs are suggested, one for each respective specification. For 38.213 it is proposed to specify the agreed remaining case for HP/LP PUSCH overlap with data and SP-CSI and for 38.214 it is suggested to clarify that it only applies for overlap between SP-CSI and data carried by two PUSCHs of the same physical layer priority. The above mentioned solution had almost reached consensus during last meeting but could in the end not be agreed due to the concerns raised by one company. The reason for concern that was brought forward was that if a clarification for TS 38.214 would be introduced, then this should be done for all cases of PUSCH overlap that appear in other sections, not only for the overlap with SP-CSI that is addressed in Section 5.2.5. Last meeting, not enough time was available and the other cases could not be assessed. In this paper, we therefore also analyze the other remaining cases of PUSCH overlap that can be found in TS 38.214 and evaluate if they need any clarification. It is found that all other cases naturally apply to any PHY priority and no clarification should be given for them. The only situation where resolving PUSCH overlap should be confined to the same PHY priority is for SP-CSI vs data, which enhances the need for a clarifying correction in TS 38.214.

